request.user_message:
Abstract the following semantic predicate cluster into exactly one reusable predicate.

Cluster ID:
unary-015

Cluster Arity:
1

Cluster Members:
[
  {
    "name": "RESTRICTS_MODIFICATION_SCOPE",
    "definition": "The reasoning explicitly limits intended changes to artifacts identified as affected and preserves or avoids modifying artifacts that are not identified as affected or relevant.",
    "parameters": [
      {
        "name": "reasoning",
        "type": "reasoning",
        "description": "The reasoning node stating the boundary of intended modifications."
      }
    ],
    "assertion_conditions": [
      "The reasoning identifies which artifacts should be modified or which should remain unchanged.",
      "The reasoning expresses a constraint to avoid altering artifacts that are not affected or relevant."
    ],
    "exclusion_conditions": [
      "The reasoning gives no indication of modification boundaries.",
      "The reasoning proposes broad changes without distinguishing affected from unaffected artifacts."
    ]
  },
  {
    "name": "ASSESSES_RESIDUAL_STORAGE_RISK",
    "definition": "The reasoning considers whether target artifacts or values may persist in non-primary or historical storage locations, such as version-control history, caches, compressed objects, or generated copies, beyond the directly visible or edited files.",
    "parameters": [
      {
        "name": "reasoning",
        "type": "reasoning",
        "description": "The reasoning node evaluating possible residual or hidden occurrences."
      }
    ],
    "assertion_conditions": [
      "The reasoning mentions a storage location or artifact class other than the directly edited working files.",
      "The reasoning evaluates whether target values may remain there or whether that location falls within the remediation scope."
    ],
    "exclusion_conditions": [
      "The reasoning only considers visible working files.",
      "The reasoning does not mention historical, cached, compressed, generated, or other non-primary storage as a possible source of residual occurrences."
    ]
  }
]

Previously Generated Predicate Names:
["CONFIGURES_EVENT_DRIVEN_AUTOMATION", "PREVENTS_SELF_CAUSED_ADVERSE_EFFECTS_THROUGH_CORRECTIVE_ACTION", "EVALUATES_CANDIDATE_AGAINST_ENUMERATED_CONSTRAINTS_OR_SCENARIOS", "RESOLVES_EVALUATED_CANDIDATE_ELEMENTS_TO_SINGLE_RESULT", "INTERPRETS_REQUIREMENTS_FOR_ACTION_ADMISSIBILITY", "INITIATES_DETACHED_ASYNCHRONOUS_EXECUTION", "REPORTS_ABSENT_OR_UNAVAILABLE_CAPABILITY", "IDENTIFIES_SPECIFIC_POTENTIAL_FAILURE_MODE", "ASSESSES_COMPETING_ACCOUNTS_OF_SAME_OBSERVATION", "ESTABLISHES_EVIDENCE_GROUNDED_TASK_OUTCOME_REFERENCE", "FORMULATES_STRUCTURED_OPERATIVE_ACCOUNT", "SPECIFIES_TARGET_LINKED_CONCRETE_MEANS", "GROUNDS_COMPUTATIONAL_ASSESSMENT_IN_QUANTITATIVE_ANALYSIS", "ANTICIPATES_PROSPECTIVE_VERIFICATION"]

Read every member's complete definition, ordered parameters, assertion conditions, and exclusion conditions. Identify the common underlying behavioral mechanism and generate exactly one complete predicate following the system instructions. The new predicate must preserve the cluster arity. Use a unique predicate name that does not conflict with previously generated predicate names. Return only the complete five-field JSON predicate.

message.content:
{
  "name": "DELIMITS_MODIFICATION_AND_RESIDUAL_ARTIFACT_SCOPE",
  "definition": "The reasoning establishes and evaluates the boundary of an intended artifact modification or remediation by distinguishing affected, in-scope artifacts or values from unaffected, preserved, or out-of-scope ones and, when persistence outside the primary working set is relevant, by assessing whether affected artifacts or values may occur in non-primary, historical, cached, generated, or otherwise residual locations that must be included in or excluded from the scope.",
  "parameters": [
    {
      "name": "reasoning",
      "type": "reasoning",
      "description": "The reasoning node that states the modification or remediation boundary and evaluates affected, preserved, and residual artifact or value occurrences."
    }
  ],
  "assertion_conditions": [
    "The reasoning identifies which artifacts or values are intended to be modified or remediated and which are to remain unchanged, unaffected, or outside the relevant scope.",
    "The reasoning evaluates coverage of the stated scope by either assessing whether affected artifacts or values may persist in non-primary, historical, cached, generated, or residual locations that should be included or excluded, or explicitly confining modification or remediation to the identified affected artifacts while leaving other artifacts unchanged."
  ],
  "exclusion_conditions": [
    "The reasoning enumerates artifacts, files, or storage locations without stating or evaluating whether they fall within or outside the modification or remediation scope.",
    "The reasoning proposes changes to artifacts without distinguishing affected from unaffected or preserved artifacts.",
    "The reasoning mentions non-primary storage only incidentally without treating it as possible residual occurrences relevant to scope."
  ]
}

